  "design_notes": "Primly reads as a tall white post on a flat square plate: a slim locker column 1.35 m high with a small square head, flanked by two long rigid arms that end in flat push-broom slabs, so from any distance it is a ruler with two brooms. Every shape is square, centred and symmetric, with crisp bevels, straight trim bands and a neatly lidded dustbin on its back, so its body literally performs its logic of keeping everything at right angles and in its place. The wide low sweeper base with hidden wheels lets it glide in perfectly straight lines, and the grey bristle skirts make even its movement look like tidying. Its palette is near-spotless clean white and pale sky blue with almost no wear or dirt, a cool white eye-light, and tiny safety-yellow lamps that tie it to Gridhaven's street language, which makes it pop sharply against the deep greens and bark browns of the Old Grove it keeps trying to tidy."
}